# {{.Name}} ({{.Type}})

Manages one local host user without managing its password. This is a system-scoped resource and may manage any literal local user; provider `target_user` is not required and does not restrict `name`.

To bootstrap a user that will later own user-scoped resources, use a two-step apply because provider configuration cannot depend on a resource from the same configuration:

```shell
terraform apply -target=host_user.target
terraform apply
```

For the first apply, either use a system-only provider and add `target_user` afterward, or configure both `target_user` and an explicit `home_dir` so the provider can initialize before the account exists.

